you should definitely be spending more  time indoors right now and you may even  have some more time on your hands to get  through that playstation pile of shame  here's a rundown of the 10 best rated  games for ps4  as gathered by review aggregator  metacritic  fyi we included some games that appeared  later on pc  and mobile but we did discount the ones  that appear on other home  consoles sorry xbox but if you'd like to  see an  xbox version of this list then make sure  to like this video and subscribe  kicking off the list with an old sega  classic res  infinite an on-rails music shooter that  originally came out in 2001  but was expanded and improved for  playstation 4.  res infinite is a technicolor marvel  hurtling you through cyberspace as you  shoot through a world of color and  music if you want to turn the intensity  down just a notch  you can even head into the new area x to  create music of your very own  if you own a psvr headset you owe it to  yourself  to try res infinite it might be  surprising to see not one  but two vr games in this list but really  it's a testament to sony's gamble on  affordable console based vr  paying off in at number nine is the  adorable astro bot rescue mission  which is sitting pretty with a meta  score of 90. not only is it a great  implementation of vr where the camera is  controlled by your head  but rescue bot is also a wonderful  platformer in its own right  featuring the absolutely adorable astro  bot  you may think that shadow of the  colossus is cheating a bit as the game  was originally made for the playstation  2 by team  ico but that would completely undermine  the incredible work done by blue point  games  in recreating the game for playstation  4. they managed to capture the haunting  spirit of the original game as well as  modernize it for a whole new audience  not only did they remake the assets so  the game would look  better but they also reconfigured the  controls to make them more in line with  what a modern audience would expect  there's a reason that shadow of the  colossus is as iconic today  as it was when it was first released so  if it passed you by  there's never been a better time to try  it out  oh i know i know you think now to tell  me that bloodborne is too  intimidating to play you've heard that  it's tough  and it's put you off well let me be the  one to tell you that if you can push  through that mindset  you'll experience one of the absolute  best games in playstation  history no other developer empowers  players through trial and error as well  as from software and bloodborne  is in my eyes their best work by  removing shields from the equation  indeed even going so far as to put a  terrible one in the game as a joke  fromsoft forced players to get up close  and personal  with the foul beasts of yanum again and  again  until their prey was slaughtered quite  thrilling  we would be remiss not to include  journey on this list  yes it came out on playstation 3 but was  also re-released for playstation 4.  it's not just one of the best  playstation games of all time  it's one of the best games of all time  period  we gave it our game of the year award in  2012.  through simple mechanics gorgeous  visuals and achingly beautiful music  it manages to deliver one of the best  video game experiences  you'll ever have it sounds like  hyperbole but  try it it's a beautiful serene  experience  from start to finish fair warning this  won't be the last time you see  a game by naughty dog on this list after  being the poster boy for the playstation  3  fans couldn't wait to see nathan drake  in a new adventure on ps4  a thief's end does what uncharted does  best  mixing bombastic action set pieces wise  cracks and treasure hunting  making nathan drake's ps4 adventure  easily his best  gamespot awarded it an elusive 10 out of  10 specifically calling out the  narrative that naughty dog had built in  the game  making nate feel less like a bullet  hungry action hero  and way more like an actual human being  i bet you didn't expect to see another  naughty dog game quite so soon but seven  years after the launch of the original  game which is oft cited as one of the  best games of all time  we finally got a sequel to the last of  us  set five years after the original game  ellie is on a relentless journey to  deliver justice to those who have  wronged her  and the quiet life she has managed to  build bigger and more brutal in every  way the last of us part 2 will likely go  down in history  as one of the playstation 4's swan song  titles  at number three is god of four sorry  war kratos had long been a playstation  icon for his blades of chaos and love  of smacking up some greek gods no one  expected a more nuanced take on the  character when the series arrived on ps4  in 2018.  the angry demi-god had left the greek  gods and their squabbles behind  and made a new life for himself in the  norse realms  where he had a wife and boy  to care for replacing the iconic blades  for an axe that you could throw and  would then return to you at the touch of  a button and adding in an emotional  story packed to the brim with action set  pieces  made god of war a remarkable and  brilliant reimagining  of the franchise a real show of force  from naughty dog on this list grabbing  the number two spot with the last of us  remastered  yes technically cheating because the  last of us originally released on  playstation 3 a year prior  but remastered did make meaningful  changes to an already incredible game  adding dualshock 4 integration a photo  mode  improved graphics and even developer  commentaries  the remastered package also threw in the  left behind dlc  which artfully examined ellie's  relationship with riley  joel and ellie's journey across a  post-pandemic america is as  heartbreaking as it is  tense and the game is considered by many  to elevate what video games can be  do yourself a favor and play it  in at number one is persona 5 royal  funnily enough persona 5 actually would  have appeared on this list  twice but we made an executive decision  not to include the base version of the  game in favor of  royal which is the definitive version  royal takes an already incredible  turn-based rpg social simulator  and improves upon it in so many ways  adding a new semester at shoojin academy  dungeon as well as characters story  elements and  gameplay tweaks to make an already  stunning battle system  sing let's do this senpai  [Music]  the enemy readings have decreased that's  gamespot awarded it 10 out of 10 with  reviewer michael hyam calling the game  a collection of small inspiring stories  an ambitious harrowing journey with some  good friends  a stunning visual and auditory  experience and a resounding call to  action  it's also absolutely worth checking out  the game's soundtrack which was recently  released on spotify  now if that doesn't get you to play it i  don't know what will  for deeper dives into some of the games  listed check out our episodes of audio  logs we did with the team at blue point  about shadow of the colossus  or with shigenori sojima about the  changes atlas made  to persona 5 royal and don't forget for  that xbox video make sure to like this  one  and subscribe to the channel i'm on  twitter at lucy james games  i'll catch you next time  you
 

